hls: an init section the list cannot take is freed, the list kept; its errors told apart

new_init_section() added the section with dynarray_add(), which, when it
cannot grow the list, frees the list, sets it to NULL and its count to 0,
and returns nothing: the section was returned all the same, not in the
list, and the sections listed before leaked. Its callers that then drop
the section just added (an EXT-X-MAP key address that is invalid or
could not be copied, and 0103's dedup_init_section()) read
init_sections[-1] of that NULL list: a crash at address -8.

Add it with av_dynarray_add_nofree() and check it: on failure the list
is kept and the section freed. drop_last_init_section() leaves an empty
list alone; it is only called after a section was added, and a broken
invariant should not abort the process playing the stream (an
av_assert0) nor index the list.

new_init_section() returned NULL for an EXT-X-MAP without a URI, with an
address that does not resolve or with an invalid BYTERANGE as for a
failed allocation, and the caller reported them all as ENOMEM. Under
0102 a local error fails a live playlist at once, while a garbled answer
is played through for live_reload_timeout: one garbled EXT-X-MAP on a
reload ended the playlist. It now returns AVERROR_INVALIDDATA for those
and AVERROR(ENOMEM) only for a failed allocation, which, on a live
reload, still fails the playlist at once (it used to play on with a
leaked section, or crash as above).

